 # Bounded Capacitor feasibility — Phase 9 Slice 1
 
+## Phase 15A Share source checkpoint — 2026-10-08
+
+The same Capacitor application receives image `ACTION_SEND`/`ACTION_SEND_MULTIPLE`
+intents through `BrickVaultSharePlugin` and the shared React review. Brian explicitly
+chooses an existing/new Marketplace Listing before Phase 13 uploads. Unknown Share
+pixels request restricted-only privacy; original bytes, receipt identity and intended
+positions remain unchanged. No capture/overlay/accessibility service is added.
+
+Intake is bounded to eight entries, 50 MiB total raw bytes and 25 MiB per file. Provider
+metadata/streams are accessed only after session verification in the foreground.
+Native and JavaScript custody is volatile; same-process activity/WebView recreation
+recovers exact queue UUID/order after authenticated listing readback, with explicit
+retry only. Selection/create uncertainty and failed-item retirement survive that
+recreation. Process death retains no private draft and cannot replay the original intent.
+Clear/logout/expiry releases unsaved custody; retained server images are not deleted.
+
+**PARTIAL — SOURCE READY / PHYSICAL DEVICE REQUIRED.** Focused source tests, lint
+and the localhost TEST APK build pass; no phone installation/Share qualification has
+run. The APK is under `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`; its receipt
+and [Plan 108](../../docs/plans/108-phase-15-android-share-capture.md) identify the exact
+artifact. Do not substitute a build or unit test for the physical acceptance checklist.
+15B capture and 15C polish remain separately gated.
+
 ## Phase 12 P12-01 production Android source path — 2026-09-28
 
 Phase 9's localhost TLS certificate and USB reverse rule were TEST-only.
